# builder: the argument [builder-finish b] passed to [fn [let _] ...] is never forced.
# LLT wraps all call arguments as Unevaluated thunks; since _ is never referenced
# in the body, the outer [builder-finish b] is never materialized.
# The body calls [builder-finish b] once on an unfinished builder, returning Dict({}).
[call [fn [let b]
    [call [fn [let _]
        [builder-finish b]]
    [builder-finish b]]]
 [make-builder]]
=== out
Dict({})
